A target in the output block may carry options, and `bubbletea(test=true)` is
one: it lowers the `testInitialCountIsZero` declaration into a `model_test.go`
beside the model, which is the second file in the golden.

That spelling generated nothing until OptionField resolved a const. `true` is
a library const rather than a literal, so `OptionBool(req.Options, "test")`
saw a non-literal and answered false, while `--opt test=true`, which parses
the string itself, worked throughout. The fixture passed either way with only
the model to look at -- the missing file is exactly what a golden shows and a
grep cannot.
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:test"

output(test=true) { go { bubbletea() } }

component main node {
    var count = 0
    button(text="+", @click { count += 1 })
    text(value="x")
}

func testInitialCountIsZero(t Test, c main) {
    t.assert(c.count == 0)
}

window {
    main
}
-- out/go/bubbletea/model.go --
